WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.701 --> 00:00:05.267
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:11.467
Pundits, I keep getting
that one wrong.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:13.601
I keep putting the second N
in there, pundits.

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.567
I know I'm doing it.
Can't stop.

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:19.300
Might just be a thing
we all have to live with.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.567
Raquel Welch.

00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:24.634
Not Welsh.

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.400
Bank.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.434
Suntan? Santander?

00:00:30.434 --> 00:00:32.167
Whatever --
that might not be right.

00:00:32.167 --> 00:00:35.734
But what I did
was definitely not right.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:37.968
Those are just some quick ones
off the top.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.501
We talked about Olive Garden.

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:42.801
We talked about the slogan,

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.334
when you're here,
you're family.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:45.667
A lot of you pointed out

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.701
that Olive Garden
had given the rights

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:51.934
to that slogan to Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:51.934 --> 00:00:54.667
So I corrected myself.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.734
And I let you all know
that last week.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:03.000
Then the correction on that
was that in 2018,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.167
Jimmy Fallon gifted

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.734
when you're here,
you're family

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:09.467
to Post Malone

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:10.934
who is a fan
of the Olive Garden.

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:13.234
They went they did a segment at
the Olive Garden and Post Malone

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.334
now has the rights to
when you're here, you're family.

00:01:15.334 --> 00:01:19.501
Then there was a loophole
that allowed the Olive Garden

00:01:19.501 --> 00:01:22.434
to take a Post Malone lyric

00:01:22.434 --> 00:01:25.367
for their new slogan.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.200
Which is Olive Garden,

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.834
I've been [bleep] hos
and popping pillys.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.667
Which is such a 180

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:39.834
from when you're here,
you're family,

00:01:39.834 --> 00:01:42.667
when you think about it.

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:44.934
I can imagine them going to
their ad agency

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:46.734
and saying,
"We want to freshen it up

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:48.834
and getting like we got
the noodles or something."

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:51.601
But...

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:57.033
Also outside just the language,

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.200
it's the pronoun.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.567
It starts I, who's the I?

00:02:01.567 --> 00:02:05.400
Like the Olive Garden,
there's not a...

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.367
It's not like Long John --
if it was Long John Silvers,

00:02:08.367 --> 00:02:11.267
you'd be like, he's --
it's he is the one

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:14.067
who's been doing this, who has
this and has been doing this.

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:23.033
Speaking of dining
establishments,

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:28.000
Subway, we were talking about

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.067
Joe Biden getting asked about
will inflation be a liability

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.434
in the upcoming election?

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:37.367
We made a joke about inflation,

00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:41.133
saying it will be hard
to get elected

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:44.501
if Subway's selling $6
foot-longs.

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:47.234
A play on $5 foot-longs.

00:02:47.234 --> 00:02:52.801
Well, turns out there haven't
been $5 foot-longs for a while.

00:02:52.801 --> 00:02:56.133
And many of you called me

00:02:56.133 --> 00:03:00.334
out of touch for not knowing

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:02.801
what a foot-long cost now.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.901
This is embarrassing.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:09.434
And I --
because I do go to Subway.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:12.534
And I'm going to probably get
in trouble for even saying this.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:20.200
Okay, so when you officially --
the year you become famous,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.801
prices freeze.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.267
I don't agree with it.

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.701
I don't think
it's a good thing, but I --

00:03:28.701 --> 00:03:31.767
in 2008, a council
of other famous people,

00:03:31.767 --> 00:03:35.434
it's all above board,
voted me in.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:40.367
So those are my prices.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.167
And I try -- I go
when I go to Subway,

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:45.033
I'm like,
let me just pay what it is now.

00:03:45.033 --> 00:03:47.534
And they're like, no, no,
no, no, Mr. Meyer.

00:03:47.534 --> 00:03:49.734
They refuse like the people
who work there.

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:51.701
And then I'll say, look,
I'll just do it, let me give you

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:54.501
and then I see in their eyes,
I get the sense.

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:59.601
That it's punitive on them

00:03:59.601 --> 00:04:01.434
if they charge me
the modern day prices.

00:04:01.434 --> 00:04:03.400
Anyway,
I don't agree with it.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.334
Oh, and also this is cool
speaking of Subway.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.467
NBC just bought Eat Fresh

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:10.601
for the Nightly News
with Lester Holt.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.934
We said that
Donald Trump never even noticed

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:21.167
when there was a red dotted line

00:04:21.167 --> 00:04:23.334
under his misspellings
on Twitter.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.834
A lot of you said
it's a red squiggly line.

00:04:26.834 --> 00:04:28.834
I think it's a dotted line
on Twitter

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.901
and a squiggly line
on Microsoft Word.

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:34.667
Maybe I'm wrong, but that's how
I've always understood it to be.

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.067
So it would like all --
if you jackals

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:41.000
Can check on that and get back
to me and admit you were wrong,

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.734
that would be nice.

00:04:45.501 --> 00:04:47.734
Okay, so.

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.067
Showed a picture
of Rudy Giuliani.

00:04:50.067 --> 00:04:53.934
And we said we've been using
this picture for so long

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:57.868
that it's gotten dusty
and I blew the dust off it.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:05:00.767
The biggest correction by far.

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.133
On that night's
"Closer Look" is

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:04.100
if you've been using it
so often,

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:05.834
it wouldn't have dust on it.

00:05:08.267 --> 00:05:10.100
Here's why that was hard
for me to read.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.701
We run "Closer Look"
back at the dressing room

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.400
before the show every night
with Wally

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.934
holding the cards and Wally,

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:21.367
and there is a rule,
Wally is not

00:05:21.367 --> 00:05:23.367
to give notes on
"A Closer Look."

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.234
But Wally said,
basically, what you said.

00:05:29.234 --> 00:05:33.300
If you used it so often,
why would there be dust on it?

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:37.534
And probably just
to be stubborn,

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.834
we said no, Wally,
it's an old joke.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:43.033
The idea is we've used it
so much, it's become old.

00:05:43.033 --> 00:05:46.701
There is therefore dust
on the oldness of the joke.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.567
Obviously, you all took
Wally side.

00:05:48.567 --> 00:05:51.067
So Wally, I would like --

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:53.033
I owe you an apology,
I'm very sorry.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.367
That's not to say, Wally

00:05:57.367 --> 00:06:01.267
is pitching a perfect game
this week.

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:05.100
We do an annual Zoom meeting

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:11.100
at NBC called respect
in the workplace,

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.501
and it's very helpful for us.

00:06:15.501 --> 00:06:20.567
Because we are now more than
ever in a corporate culture.

00:06:20.567 --> 00:06:22.567
It's very important for people
to respect one another.

00:06:22.567 --> 00:06:26.100
And it was on Zoom
and, you know,

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:29.767
I think a few of us
ended up on gallery view.

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:33.000
And again, not everybody
here is back at work.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:37.434
So it's a nice way to look
at people's apartments

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:40.734
and say, well,

00:06:40.734 --> 00:06:43.968
here's Wally, you guys.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:48.434
There.

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:53.200
That's how Wally decided
to respect the workplace.

00:06:57.801 --> 00:07:00.534
And with that said,

00:07:00.534 --> 00:07:03.901
we give Wally
a lot of grief here.

00:07:03.901 --> 00:07:06.901
But no one works harder

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:10.868
than Wally physically
on our entire crew,

00:07:10.868 --> 00:07:12.133
because Wally does hold --

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:14.667
when you see him,
he is holding cue cards

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.467
and sometimes especially
with "A Closer Look,"

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:18.200
it can be a lot of cue cards.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.767
And Wally's got to pull them

00:07:19.767 --> 00:07:22.033
and he's got to do it
in perfect cadence

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:22.901
with how I'm speaking.

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:24.234
He's the best in the biz,

00:07:24.234 --> 00:07:27.167
and I'm -- sometimes that
makes me mad that we act like

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:30.100
Wally isn't the most
valued member of our staff

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:32.968
because we got a lot of really
strapping guys in our crew.

00:07:32.968 --> 00:07:34.901
And from what I can tell,
they don't do [bleep].

00:07:37.567 --> 00:07:39.834
Like for real like big guys

00:07:39.834 --> 00:07:41.100
and they're like,
I'm a camera guy.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.367
All the --
everything's on wheels.

00:07:46.467 --> 00:07:47.968
I mean,
we have this big guy, Kenny,

00:07:47.968 --> 00:07:51.033
and he just like, he's got like,
maybe like a cord.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:57.701
And Wally, like, is holding
physical stuff and we call --

00:07:57.701 --> 00:08:00.200
and I mean the thing --
like we all call

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:03.634
everybody here like their name

00:08:03.634 --> 00:08:06.100
and like what they move around.

00:08:06.100 --> 00:08:10.100
So it's like Wally Cue Card,
Paul Camera, Kenny Coyle.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.300
So the fact is, Wally works
harder than everybody else.

00:08:20.300 --> 00:08:22.400
And that's why I had
to tell everybody,

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.801
hey, you guys all think
Wally's at home, but he's not.

00:08:24.801 --> 00:08:27.133
This is -- we built him a room
with a bed

00:08:27.133 --> 00:08:29.067
because he works so hard.

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:31.601
And while he said, you know,
I'm so tired and I'm worried

00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:34.000
I'm going to drop the cards
and can you get me?

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.534
And we said, we're going
to get your room with a bed.

00:08:35.534 --> 00:08:37.667
And he said, great,
I-I picked out a headboard.

00:08:37.667 --> 00:08:39.367
And we were like, what?

00:08:41.434 --> 00:08:43.534
Okay.

00:08:43.534 --> 00:08:47.200
But, you know,
the people didn't know.

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:49.033
The people didn't know on
the call,

00:08:49.033 --> 00:08:52.934
especially, you know,
the sort of the woman

00:08:52.934 --> 00:08:54.934
who is running
the meeting who is,

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:56.834
you know, a legal expert
on this sort of thing.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:08:58.734
And I felt like
she was worried about Wally

00:08:58.734 --> 00:09:01.100
because all
her questions started

00:09:01.100 --> 00:09:03.801
I felt like leading towards that
because the questions like,

00:09:03.801 --> 00:09:06.367
what would you do at work if,

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:09.667
you know, someone said something
inappropriate about your dress?

00:09:09.667 --> 00:09:12.133
And then the next hypothetical
was like, what would you --

00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:14.300
would you blink your eyes
if your wife poisoned you

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.067
and you were paralyzed
in your bed?

00:09:23.734 --> 00:09:27.367
Anyways,
Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles,

00:09:27.367 --> 00:09:33.234
I guess I keep calling
them bandanas and...

00:09:33.234 --> 00:09:34.968
they're masks.

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:36.968
I was told stop
calling them bandanas.

00:09:36.968 --> 00:09:38.267
They wear masks,

00:09:38.267 --> 00:09:42.834
although Donatello
just stopped wearing his mask

00:09:42.834 --> 00:09:45.400
because last he checked,
this was America.

00:09:53.567 --> 00:09:58.133
We had a note, like in a high
school middle school notebook

00:09:58.133 --> 00:10:02.167
two weeks ago,
now spelled later L-8-T-E-R.

00:10:02.167 --> 00:10:04.234
A lot of people said
you don't need the T.

00:10:04.234 --> 00:10:06.701
So corrected it to L-A-E-R.

00:10:06.701 --> 00:10:08.167
And then a bunch of people,
which would have been

00:10:08.167 --> 00:10:09.701
[bleep] helpful
the first week said

00:10:09.701 --> 00:10:11.167
you also don't need the E.

00:10:11.167 --> 00:10:12.834
L-8-R.

00:10:12.834 --> 00:10:15.167
So now I know it's L-8-R.

00:10:15.167 --> 00:10:18.133
And then if you want to do
later hater -- L-8-R H-8-R.

00:10:18.133 --> 00:10:21.033
So now I'm more than ready
to pass myself off

00:10:21.033 --> 00:10:24.400
as a youth in 1999.

00:10:26.434 --> 00:10:28.367
Got S Club Seven tickets.

00:10:30.834 --> 00:10:31.968
I'm not even going to repeat it

00:10:31.968 --> 00:10:33.901
because
it's very upsetting to people.

00:10:33.901 --> 00:10:37.467
We told a cat joke.
Very cool cat joke.

00:10:37.467 --> 00:10:40.100
And then I reference it again

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:43.300
last week in corrections,

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.200
and I just want to first of all,
I want to stress

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:47.534
because I think
I come off as a cat hater.

00:10:47.534 --> 00:10:50.434
I don't write these jokes.

00:10:50.434 --> 00:10:54.400
The person who writes
these jokes is a cat owner.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.334
And he has a cat
who's 18 years old.

00:10:57.334 --> 00:11:00.367
So he would never hurt a cat.

00:11:00.367 --> 00:11:03.567
He would just apparently
fantasize about it.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.801
I think one of the problems
and I also,

00:11:08.801 --> 00:11:12.167
I think, came off snobbily
is a dog person.

00:11:12.167 --> 00:11:14.334
And that's why I think
people hate cats.

00:11:14.334 --> 00:11:17.567
That's not true. The reason
I think that is I have a dog

00:11:17.567 --> 00:11:21.067
who looks like a cat
and people hate my dog.

00:11:23.734 --> 00:11:27.634
But I do want
to make this right.

00:11:27.634 --> 00:11:29.434
Because a bunch of people

00:11:29.434 --> 00:11:31.667
pointed out
another group of people

00:11:31.667 --> 00:11:34.334
that I've run afoul of
is the knitting community.

00:11:34.334 --> 00:11:36.334
And they said

00:11:36.334 --> 00:11:37.567
you should have learned

00:11:37.567 --> 00:11:39.067
your lesson in
the knitting community.

00:11:39.067 --> 00:11:41.400
The next group
you don't want to run afoul of

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.968
is the cat community,

00:11:42.968 --> 00:11:45.934
although I bet there
is some overlap.

00:11:55.701 --> 00:11:59.400
Talked about Thomas Jefferson

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.400
having to make --

00:12:01.400 --> 00:12:05.033
having to invent
an excuse to his wife, Martha,

00:12:05.033 --> 00:12:09.067
about why Sally Hemings' kids
had his eyes

00:12:09.067 --> 00:12:11.133
and this was --
somebody sent this in.

00:12:11.133 --> 00:12:13.534
This is sometimes
I like to print out the facts

00:12:13.534 --> 00:12:15.634
so I can read them

00:12:15.634 --> 00:12:19.534
exactly as they were written,

00:12:19.534 --> 00:12:23.067
which is Martha Jefferson
died in 1782

00:12:23.067 --> 00:12:24.767
and Sally Hemings
first child wasn't born

00:12:24.767 --> 00:12:26.834
until 1795,
so it wasn't an affair,

00:12:26.834 --> 00:12:28.868
nor would she ever
have seen the children.

00:12:28.868 --> 00:12:32.167
Also, Hemings was
Martha Jefferson's half-sister,

00:12:32.167 --> 00:12:34.734
which means that all of
Thomas Jefferson's children

00:12:34.734 --> 00:12:37.734
were both half-siblings
and cousins.

00:12:37.734 --> 00:12:39.534
Fun!

00:12:41.801 --> 00:12:44.534
How was
the family reunion? Bad!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.167
Oh, this I forgot to read
this one just again,

00:12:50.167 --> 00:12:53.667
this is not...

00:12:53.667 --> 00:12:56.033
Someone wrote this
as a joke my grandfather

00:12:56.033 --> 00:12:59.067
used to say this is about --

00:12:59.067 --> 00:13:02.000
about the cats.

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:03.200
My grandfather used to say,

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:06.334
if you guess how many cats
are in "dis" bag,

00:13:06.334 --> 00:13:08.234
I'll give you
the "boat of dem."

00:13:13.467 --> 00:13:17.167
Oh, we talked about --
oh, by the way,

00:13:17.167 --> 00:13:19.133
I referred
to Martha Jefferson.

00:13:19.133 --> 00:13:21.968
This was an exchange
I had to read in corrections.

00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:26.400
I can't believe
Seth thinks Thomas Jefferson

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.501
was married to Martha Washington
and someone else said

00:13:30.501 --> 00:13:33.033
Thomas Jefferson's wife
was also named Martha.

00:13:33.033 --> 00:13:34.834
And then the first person said,

00:13:34.834 --> 00:13:37.834
yeah, but Seth probably
doesn't know that.

00:13:41.801 --> 00:13:44.601
Prince Andrew.

00:13:44.601 --> 00:13:48.734
We talked about Prince Andrew,
and I guess he's --

00:13:48.734 --> 00:13:52.200
well, I can say this,
he's had to rescind

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.734
his royal titles
because of...

00:13:55.734 --> 00:13:58.467
And -- and now, so now,

00:13:58.467 --> 00:14:01.100
you have to refer to him
as the royal...

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:06.901
formerly known as Prince Andrew,
and you you spell it like this.

00:14:16.501 --> 00:14:21.567
We referenced a writer of ours

00:14:21.567 --> 00:14:22.934
qualifying as a serial killer

00:14:22.934 --> 00:14:26.834
because they wrote
two terrible jokes in a row.

00:14:26.834 --> 00:14:29.267
It's got it -- so in order to be
a serial killer,

00:14:29.267 --> 00:14:31.801
it's got to be three.

00:14:31.801 --> 00:14:34.167
I guess if it's only two,
it can still legally

00:14:34.167 --> 00:14:36.067
be classified
as a coincidence.

00:14:38.267 --> 00:14:42.234
And I guess the reason they did
that is because --

00:14:42.234 --> 00:14:44.334
you have to kill three
before you're a serial killer,

00:14:44.334 --> 00:14:45.734
